# 8. Proof Architecture

A possible proof program is:

$$
b(T)\ge q+1
$$

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Choose a suitable maximal failed \(q\)-round burning sequence.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Study the last unburned component.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Prove a **branching-compensation lemma** showing that a persistent obstruction can be pushed away from branching vertices.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

The obstruction must propagate through degree-2 corridors.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Track the obstruction backward through the previous rounds.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Show that each additional persistence layer requires two previously unused degree-2 vertices.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Obtain

$$
2(q-1)
$$

vertices.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

Show that the final surviving obstruction requires one additional degree-2 vertex.

$$
\Downarrow
$$

$$
n_2(T)\ge2q-1.
$$

### Explicitly unproved steps

The two essential gaps are:

$$
\boxed{
\text{branching-compensation/source-rerouting}
}
$$

and

$$
\boxed{
\text{two-new-degree-2-vertices-per-persistence-layer}.
}
$$

Neither is established.

