# 10. What the Existing Computations Actually Support

### [DIRECTLY FROM DATA]

The existing computation supports the following finite observations:

1. No actual-\(q\) obstruction was found for \(n\le19\).
2. Boundary trees with \(b=q\) have many different topological cores.
3. Balanced long-arm structures can produce increases in burning number in the \(K_{1,9}\) subdivision family.
4. The known balanced-arm family \(T_r\) has

   $$
   n_2=(r-1)(r-2),
   $$

   which is much larger than \(2r-1\).

Therefore the \(T_r\) family illustrates a **local obstruction mechanism**, but not the sharp global threshold.

